From f15898c374826f88d4bb59fcdd86a66df23f0191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HIPC AI Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:45:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] convert: add --proposal-ids for an explicit proposal
 (draft) vocabulary

The indexed proposal head used by --lm-head-draft is a frequency shortlist
built from the bundled en/zh/code/math ranking. For other languages that
shortlist misses many output tokens (Korean: 131072 rows cover only 58-71%
of Korean text tokens), so MTP/DFlash drafts for those tokens can never be
accepted.

--proposal-ids FILE (.npy or whitespace/comma separated text) selects the
proposal rows directly; special tokens are still forced in, rows follow the
list length, and verification still uses the full output head, so outputs
are unchanged. No runtime change is needed: the engine already loads any
indexed proposal head.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
